  <story>
    <asA>developer</asA>
    <iWant>a compilation pipeline triggered after successful deployment</iWant>
    <soThat>wiki snapshots are archived, deployed code is marked, and deployment records are created for full release traceability</soThat>
    <tasks>
      <task id="1" ac="1">Create deployment completion listener
        <subtask>Hook into the deployment pipeline completion event to detect successful deploys</subtask>
        <subtask>Create generateDeployCompilePipeline() function that builds the three-step pipeline definition (shell -> agent -> shell)</subtask>
        <subtask>Enqueue the deploy-compile job to futurator-agent-jobs with projectId, PROJECT_NAME, DEPLOY_URL, and date context</subtask>
        <subtask>Emit pipeline status events for each compilation sub-step</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="2" ac="2">Implement S3 wiki snapshot shell step
        <subtask>Create shell step that tars the knowledge/ directory</subtask>
        <subtask>Upload tarball to s3://futurator-ai-website/knowledge-archives/{projectId}/{date}.tar.gz</subtask>
        <subtask>Each archive is a new file (versioned by date), never overwritten</subtask>
        <subtask>Clean up local /tmp/ tarball after successful upload</subtask>
        <subtask>Snapshot failure logs a warning but does not block remaining compilation steps</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="3" ac="3,4,5,6">Implement COMPILER agent deploy-nodes step
        <subtask>Create agent step with agentId: COMPILER and post-deployment prompt from architecture doc section 4.4</subtask>
        <subtask>Agent creates knowledge/release/deploy-{date}.md with deployment metadata and [[wikilinks]] to deployed code articles</subtask>
        <subtask>Agent marks code articles with completed epic status as status: deployed in frontmatter</subtask>
        <subtask>Agent updates knowledge/system/deployment-manifest.md with latest deploy info</subtask>
        <subtask>Agent appends deployment event to knowledge/log.md</subtask>
        <subtask>Agent updates knowledge/index.md to include the new deploy record</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="4" ac="7">Implement full graph resync with prune flag
        <subtask>Add shell step calling graph-sync.mjs with --full-resync --prune flags</subtask>
        <subtask>The --prune flag tells graph-sync to remove nodes whose articles have been moved to knowledge/archive/ (prepared for Story 3.4)</subtask>
        <subtask>Include S3 live backup of knowledge/ directory after sync</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="5" ac="3">Create knowledge/release/ directory support
        <subtask>Ensure knowledge/release/ directory is part of wiki initialization script (init-wiki.sh from Story 1.3)</subtask>
        <subtask>Define deployment record article format: type: deployment-record, phase: release, status: active</subtask>
        <subtask>Deployment record includes sections: Summary, Deployed Articles, Deploy Configuration, Release Notes</subtask>
      </task>
      <task id="6" ac="1">Error handling
        <subtask>Deploy compilation failure does NOT affect the deployment status (app is already deployed)</subtask>
        <subtask>Each step has independent error handling — snapshot failure does not block node marking</subtask>
        <subtask>Errors logged to futurator-agent-events with full context</subtask>
      </task>
    </tasks>
  </story>

  <acceptanceCriteria>
    <criterion id="1">When a deployment pipeline completes successfully (S3 sync + CloudFront invalidation), a deploy-compile pipeline job is automatically created and enqueued</criterion>
    <criterion id="2">The wiki directory is archived as a versioned tarball to s3://futurator-ai-website/knowledge-archives/{projectId}/{date}.tar.gz</criterion>
    <criterion id="3">A deployment record article is created at knowledge/release/deploy-{date}.md with: epic title, story count, deploy URL, and list of all code articles included in the deploy</criterion>
    <criterion id="4">All code articles whose epic status is completed are marked status: deployed</criterion>
    <criterion id="5">knowledge/system/deployment-manifest.md is updated with the deployment details (deploy date, URL, deployed article list)</criterion>
    <criterion id="6">knowledge/log.md records the deployment event with timestamp and summary</criterion>
    <criterion id="7">A full Memgraph resync runs after the agent step completes</criterion>
  </acceptanceCriteria>

