  <constraints>
    <constraint type="non-blocking">Deploy compilation failure MUST NOT affect the deployment status. The app is already deployed — compilation is post-processing knowledge archival and node marking.</constraint>
    <constraint type="step-independence">Each step has independent error handling. Snapshot failure does NOT block deploy-node marking. Node marking failure does NOT block graph-sync. Use onFail: { action: 'fail' } selectively.</constraint>
    <constraint type="dependency">This story depends on Epic 2 (story compilation) and Story 3.1 (epic compilation pipeline provides the pattern). It sets the stage for Story 3.4 (pruning scan).</constraint>
    <constraint type="ordering">Pipeline step order is critical: shell (snapshot) -> agent (deploy-nodes) -> shell (prune-sync). The snapshot must happen before any node status changes. The graph-sync must happen after all article updates.</constraint>
    <constraint type="archival">S3 archives are versioned by date, never overwritten. Each deployment creates a new tarball. Full history is retained for rollback of knowledge state.</constraint>
    <constraint type="release-directory">knowledge/release/ is a new directory that must be created by init-wiki.sh. Deployment record articles use type: deployment-record, phase: release.</constraint>
  </constraints>

